dropped the body
could not fully type-check
--
N5008 [temp.names]/3: within a template-argument-list the first non-nested
`>' ends the list; a `<' inside an argument is the less-than operator.
`align_it<1 < 8 ? 8 : 1>(n)' (libc++'s basic_string::__recommend, via
`__align_it<sizeof(value_type) < __alignment ? ... : 1>(__s + 1)') defeats the
parser's balanced-bracket pre-check, so the template-id is recognised by the
postfix-expression retry -- which appended the bare argument list to the name
instead of a `template_args' component.  The type checker could not read the
id-less node and the function body was dropped (108 occurrences over the
libc++ tests of the corpus).
